WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.956
Graph neural networks need many labeled nodes, and
labeling is expensive.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:07.991
This ICLR 2022 paper, Information Gain Propagation,
rethinks graph active learning.

00:00:08.071 --> 00:00:12.027
Instead of asking an oracle for a node's exact class,

00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:16.063
it asks a cheaper binary question: does this node
belong to a given class?

00:00:16.143 --> 00:00:20.099
That soft label,

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:24.134
plus a criterion picking nodes whose information
gain propagates farthest,

00:00:24.214 --> 00:00:28.170
gives higher accuracy at lower cost.
